{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"generated":true,"title":"Reference"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"EntityStore","roleHeading":"Article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" works like a dictionary with insertion-order iteration. Entities must conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID"},{"type":"text","text":" as the ID type."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var cards = EntityStore<Card>()","","cards[card.id] = card                      \/\/ Insert or update — recorded","cards.modify(card.id) { $0.title = \"New\" } \/\/ In-place — recorded only if value changes","cards[card.id] = nil                       \/\/ Delete — recorded","","let card = cards[cardID]                   \/\/ O(1) lookup","let all  = cards.values                    \/\/ Insertion-ordered array","","cards.sort { $0.sortIndex < $1.sortIndex } \/\/ Only marks moved entities","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }          \/\/ Rebuilds index in one pass"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every mutation is tracked in a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" that the middleware drains after each reducer call."}]},{"anchor":"Bulk-Deletion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bulk Deletion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"code":"cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shifts the storage array’s tail and reindexes the shifted entries — O(tail) per delete, so a loop of k subscript deletes costs O(n·k). To delete many entities at once, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(ids:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (when you have the IDs) or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll(where:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (when you have a predicate) instead: both remove everything in a single pass with one index rebuild, record the same deletions, and cancel pending upserts exactly like the subscript."}]},{"code":["cards.remove(ids: selection)          \/\/ One pass, not a subscript loop","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Merging (Re-hydration)","type":"heading","anchor":"Merging-Re-hydration","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Replacing an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" after startup destroys any in-memory state that was loaded lazily after initial hydration. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — entities only in the other store are always added, and the closure decides whether an incoming value overwrites the current one:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Absorb DB rows; take an incoming row only when the current one","\/\/ lacks lazily-computed data.","campaigns.merge(from: EntityStore(allFromDB)) { current, incoming in","    current.calculationState == nil && incoming.calculationState != nil","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge"},{"type":"text","text":" does not record changes — it has hydration semantics like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"reconcile vs merge","anchor":"reconcile-vs-merge"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two answer different questions:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcile(with:preserving:removingMissing:)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stance"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep everything, absorb what’s new","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is authoritative "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"except"}]},{"type":"text","text":" where you say otherwise"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes rows"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Never","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"code":"removingMissing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the ID isn’t preserved","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Conflicts"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your closure decides, per pair"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage wins unless the ID is preserved"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcile"},{"type":"text","text":" is what lets a remote edit or a remote deletion surface mid-session rather than waiting for the next launch. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"type":"text","text":" is the caller’s list of IDs that carry unflushed local intent; the store’s own un-drained "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"type":"text","text":" are folded in automatically, so a pending local deletion is never resurrected even when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["cards.reconcile(with: EntityStore(rowsFromDisk), preserving: dirtyIDs, removingMissing: true)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge"},{"type":"text","text":", it records no changes — every value it writes or removes already reflects what is in storage, so recording them would echo each remote change straight back as a local write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most apps never call this directly; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator.rehydrate(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does, and computes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"type":"text","text":" for you."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"restore(from:)","anchor":"restorefrom"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" replaces all entities with those from the source store while recording the diff as changes for persistence. Used by undo\/redo (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deletions"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — IDs in self but absent from source"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Upserts"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — IDs that are new or whose values differ"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unchanged"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — identical values produce no change records"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Remote deletions are not undoable","anchor":"Remote-deletions-are-not-undoable"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One class of ID is skipped: anything "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcile"},{"type":"text","text":" removed because storage no longer held it. Those IDs are kept in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remotelyRemovedIDs"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore"},{"type":"text","text":" will neither re-add them nor record a change for them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without that, undo resurrects rows other devices deleted. An undo snapshot taken before the deletion still contains the entity, so restoring it records an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"upsert"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — which flushes as a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"creation"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed the row was gone. Undo is scoped to what the local user did; a deletion made on another device isn’t that."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ID leaves the set as soon as it becomes local again — an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store[id] = entity"},{"type":"text","text":", or storage handing the row back on a later merge — so a row that another device deletes and then restores is undoable once more. The set survives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resetChanges()"},{"type":"text","text":", because a flush ends a pending write’s life, not a deletion’s."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ \"3 items were deleted on another device.\"","cards.remotelyRemovedIDs.count"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stores that never sync never populate it, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore"},{"type":"text","text":" takes exactly the path it did before."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"article","title":"Macros"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ChangeSet","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"kind":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}],"kind":"article","title":"Troubleshooting"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"kind":"article","title":"KeyValueStore"}}}